--- When log itself stops the program (here on a decimal too long to show, see
--- pi_to_1_million_digits-1.co), the lines logged before it are lost, in both modes,
--- when standard output is a pipe or a file (crow run -i x.co > out.txt):
---   prints only: runtime error: line 12: Formatting argument out of range
---   expected:    before
---                runtime error: line 12: Formatting argument out of range
--- With the failing call outside log (t = str[x]), 'before' is printed. The spec's
--- note on log's blocks: a way for a program to end flushes what was logged first;
--- a stop raised while log formats its argument does not.
x = decimal[1, digits = 70000] / decimal[3, digits = 70000]
log['before']
log[x]
log['after']
